# sds-lane-rotation-proposer's schedule: one writing pass a day at 06:31, in the image's
# America/New_York time. The Mac job runs at 06:30 (`scripts/com.devon.rotation-proposer.plist`,
# `StartCalendarInterval` 06:30, `--submit`), but minute 30 is execution-watch's (`*/15`), so the
# lane takes 31, the nearest minute no other lane uses: execution-watch runs on the quarter-hours,
# the unit verifier on 2-52/10, the work carrier on 07:05, the deploy watcher on 20, the pin watcher
# on 07:25, the landing ledger on 07:30, the change proposer on 35, the revision watcher on 40, the
# membership check on 07:47, the rotation decomposer on 50 and the bump proposer on 06:55. 06:31
# still runs before the bump proposer, which pushes to the same intent-packages `main`, and before
# the carry's 07:05. `--submit` is passed here, where it is visible, as the plist passes it: a bare
# run is the dry run, which writes nothing (and, this lane being armed, still pings its check).
# The entrypoint runs this file only when LANE_SCHEDULE_ENABLED is `true`.
31 6 * * * lane-run rotation-proposer --submit
